    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0214" n="134" xml:id="pg134"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 405.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith, for your information
                    and for an investigation and report by you of the facts of the case, a copy of a
                        note<anchor n="a" xml:id="d121-f1"/> from the Chinese minister here
                    inclosing the translation of a dispatch addressed to him by the viceroy at
                    Nanking relative to a recent rupture at Hsin-Chin between Chinese converts of
                    the American Protestant mission and those of a Roman Catholic mission.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
